<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Past speculation: <em>reconstruct without pretending to know</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">The event is over, but the evidence is incomplete. Use <span class="ex">must have</span> for a strongly supported positive conclusion, <span class="ex">may / might / could have</span> for live possibilities, and <span class="ex">can't / couldn't have</span> when reliable evidence rules an explanation out. The modal reports your present judgment, not a direct view of the past.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">70–80 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">evidence → calibrated inference</span>
    <span class="tag">modal + have + participle</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Separate</b><span>Record fact before inference.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Calibrate</b><span>Support, possibility, or contradiction.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Completed, ongoing, state, and passive forms.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Update</b><span>Revise a claim when new evidence arrives.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish a recorded past fact from a current inference about it; choose <span class="ex">must have</span>, <span class="ex">may / might / could have</span>, <span class="ex">might not have</span>, <span class="ex">must not have</span>, or <span class="ex">can't / couldn't have</span> without claiming more than the evidence supports; build active, state, continuous, passive, negative, and question forms; distinguish speculative <span class="ex">could have</span> from unrealized opportunity, counterfactual result, <span class="ex">should have</span> evaluation, and past obligation; hear weak <span class="ex">have</span> in natural U.S. speech; and give a responsible reconstruction that changes when the evidence changes.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved present deduction, possibility, contradiction, and two past participles before moving the same reasoning to an earlier time.">
    <h3>Reactivate the B1 evidence system and participles</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Past speculation foundation choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must be">must be</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might be">might be</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can't be">can't be</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="taken">taken</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="written">written</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must have">must have</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Rina signed in two minutes ago, and her equipment is beside Studio A. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must be" data-hint="Several current clues strongly support one positive location conclusion." data-fix="She must be near Studio A.">choose</button> near Studio A.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The sound could come from the studio or the hallway. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might be" data-hint="Two current locations remain possible." data-fix="She might be inside the studio.">choose</button> inside the studio.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Studio B was checked and is empty and locked. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can't be" data-hint="The checked present fact directly contradicts this location." data-fix="She can't be in Studio B.">choose</button> in Studio B.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The past participle of <span class="ex">take</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="taken" data-hint="After have, take changes to its irregular participle." data-fix="take → took → taken">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The past participle of <span class="ex">write</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="written" data-hint="After have, write changes to its irregular participle." data-fix="write → wrote → written">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: the evidence is past, but the judgment is now</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Eastport Museum archive transfer, Saturday morning</h3>
    <p><b>Recorded facts:</b> An automated transfer began at 8:00 a.m. Ten image files reached Archive A. File L-07 entered the queue at 8:06, but it has no completion entry. The network connection was down from 8:07 to 8:11. File L-08 never entered the queue. A Friday configuration snapshot excludes the West Gallery folder that contained L-08.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">L-07 must have reached the transfer queue.</span> The 8:06 entry strongly supports that conclusion.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">It might have been transferring when the connection failed.</span> The timing supports this explanation, but the log does not show the exact process state.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">L-07 can't have completed the normal transfer.</span> A completed transfer would have a completion entry, and none exists.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">The Friday settings must have omitted L-08's folder.</span> The saved snapshot strongly supports the positive conclusion.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which words are direct records, and which words are conclusions?</li>
      <li>Why is <span class="ex">must have</span> strong but still not the same as direct observation?</li>
      <li>What additional log would turn the L-07 process from a possibility into a documented fact?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated recorded facts from present conclusions, graded the claims, and kept strong inference distinct from proof.">
    <h3>Discovery check: fact, inference, and time</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Past speculation discovery choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a recorded past fact">a recorded past fact</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a strongly supported positive inference">a strongly supported positive inference</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a live past possibility">a live past possibility</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a strongly rejected past explanation">a strongly rejected past explanation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an inference rather than proof">an inference rather than proof</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a present judgment about an earlier event">a present judgment about an earlier event</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">The connection was down from 8:07 to 8:11</span> is presented as <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a recorded past fact" data-hint="The network monitor directly records this interval." data-fix="The outage interval is a recorded past fact in this fictional file.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">L-07 must have reached the queue</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a strongly supported positive inference" data-hint="The 8:06 queue entry makes this conclusion highly reasonable." data-fix="Must have presents a strongly supported positive inference.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">It might have been transferring</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a live past possibility" data-hint="The timing fits, but no process-state record confirms it." data-fix="Might have been transferring keeps a past process possible.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">L-07 can't have completed the normal transfer</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a strongly rejected past explanation" data-hint="The missing completion entry contradicts a completed normal transfer." data-fix="Can't have rejects the completed-transfer explanation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Even with strong evidence, <span class="ex">must have</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an inference rather than proof" data-hint="The speaker reasons from the record rather than directly observing the process." data-fix="Must have is a high-confidence inference, not a label that makes a claim proven.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The time relationship in <span class="ex">must have reached</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a present judgment about an earlier event" data-hint="The reaching is earlier; the speaker evaluates the evidence now." data-fix="Modal + have + participle places the inferred event before the judgment point.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: claim strength follows the evidence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A modal does not carry a universal percentage. <span class="ex">Must have</span> usually presents the speaker's best strongly supported explanation, but it is still defeasible: new evidence can overturn it. <span class="ex">May, might,</span> and epistemic <span class="ex">could have</span> keep an explanation open. <span class="ex">Can't have</span> or <span class="ex">couldn't have</span> rejects one because it conflicts with reliable evidence.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Evidence relationship</th><th>Useful form</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>strongly supports a positive conclusion</td><td><b>must have</b> + participle</td><td>The settings <b>must have omitted</b> the folder.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>keeps one or more positive explanations open</td><td><b>may / might / could have</b> + participle</td><td>The outage <b>might have interrupted</b> L-07.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>keeps nonoccurrence possible, but not certain</td><td><b>may not / might not have</b> + participle</td><td>The backup <b>might not have captured</b> the whole file.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>strongly supports a negative conclusion</td><td><b>must not have</b> + participle</td><td>The scheduler <b>must not have read</b> the excluded folder.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>rules an event or state out</td><td><b>can't / couldn't have</b> + participle</td><td>L-08 <b>can't have entered</b> the queue.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Negative conclusions need more than one simplified rule</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">Might not have entered</span> means perhaps it did not enter. The speaker leaves both outcomes open.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Must not have entered</span> is a strong inference that it did not enter. This use is natural in U.S. English: <span class="ex">He must not have seen the message.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">Can't have entered</span> presents entry as incompatible with the evidence.</li>
      <li>Contracted <span class="ex">mustn't have</span> can sound less common in U.S. speech and may be confused with prohibition. Use full <span class="ex">must not have</span> for the inference or <span class="ex">can't have</span> when the evidence rules an event out.</li>
      <li>Past prohibition is a different meaning: <span class="ex">Staff were not allowed to enter</span>. Do not assume every negative <span class="ex">must</span> form is a deduction.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Every modal now reflects the stated evidence relationship rather than a memorized certainty percentage.">
    <h3>Calibrate eight claims from complete contexts</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Evidence calibration choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must have">must have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="may have">may have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might have">might have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could have">could have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might not have">might not have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must not have">must not have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can't have">can't have</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="not enough evidence">not enough evidence</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The access record contains one valid badge ID, and the camera shows the same badge at the door. The authorized technician <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must have" data-hint="Two independent records strongly support a positive entry conclusion." data-fix="The authorized technician must have entered through that door.">choose</button> entered through that door.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The report lists two plausible export tools and does not record which one ran. The team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="may have" data-hint="One positive explanation remains possible, but it is not established." data-fix="The team may have used the desktop export tool.">choose</button> used the desktop export tool.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The door sensor briefly lost power, so it is possible that one opening was not recorded. Someone <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might have" data-hint="The power loss creates a live possibility without strong positive support." data-fix="Someone might have opened the door during the sensor outage.">choose</button> opened the door during the outage.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Three independent routes were available, and the location log is incomplete. The courier <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could have" data-hint="The route was genuinely possible, but the actual route is unknown." data-fix="The courier could have taken the service road.">choose</button> taken the service road.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The reminder system sometimes suppresses duplicate notices, but its detailed log is unavailable. The customer <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might not have" data-hint="Nonreceipt is possible, but receipt has not been ruled out." data-fix="The customer might not have received the second reminder.">choose</button> received the second reminder.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The reply asks for information stated in the first paragraph. A strong explanation is that the reader <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must not have" data-hint="The reply strongly suggests that the paragraph was not noticed, although that is still an inference." data-fix="The reader must not have noticed the first paragraph.">choose</button> noticed the first paragraph.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The signed attendance sheet places Noor in Boston at the exact time of the in-person Denver meeting. Noor <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can't have" data-hint="The verified simultaneous location contradicts physical attendance in Denver." data-fix="Noor can't have attended the Denver meeting in person.">choose</button> attended in person.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>One file is missing, and there are no logs, timestamps, backups, or witness records. The claim that a particular employee deleted it has <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="not enough evidence" data-hint="A missing result alone does not identify one mechanism or person." data-fix="There is not enough evidence to identify who or what removed the file.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the complete time and voice pattern</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The sequence after the modal is a <b>perfect infinitive</b>, not a Present Perfect tense. The modal stays unchanged. Base <span class="ex">have</span> places the situation before the judgment point, and the following form chooses the viewpoint.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Viewpoint</th><th>Form</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>completed active event</td><td>modal + <b>have + participle</b></td><td>She might have <b>left</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier state or location</td><td>modal + <b>have been</b> + complement</td><td>They must have <b>been busy</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier ongoing or repeated activity</td><td>modal + <b>have been + -ing</b></td><td>It could have <b>been transferring</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier passive event</td><td>modal + <b>have been + participle</b></td><td>The file may have <b>been moved</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>negative possibility</td><td>modal + <b>not have</b>...</td><td>She might not have <b>heard</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>yes-or-no question</td><td>modal + subject + <b>have</b>...?</td><td>Could the system have <b>restarted</b>?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>information question</td><td>wh-word + modal + subject + <b>have</b>...?</td><td>What might the outage have <b>affected</b>?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Layer checks</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A modal takes base <span class="ex">have</span>, never <span class="ex">has</span> or <span class="ex">had</span>: <span class="ex">She might have left</span>.</li>
      <li>Completed active meaning needs the lexical past participle: <span class="ex">go → gone, take → taken, write → written</span>.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Have been + -ing</span> profiles a possible process. <span class="ex">Have been + participle</span> profiles a possible passive event. The word after <span class="ex">been</span> carries the contrast.</li>
      <li>Questions invert the modal and subject. Do not add <span class="ex">did</span>: <span class="ex">Could it have failed?</span>, not <span class="ex">Did it could have failed?</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You preserved the modal, base have, viewpoint layer, lexical form, negation, and question order in ten distinct past inferences.">
    <h3>Choose the exact active, state, continuous, passive, negative, or question form</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Past speculation form choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must have left">must have left</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might not have saved">might not have saved</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could have been waiting">could have been waiting</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must have been closed">must have been closed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="may have been copied">may have been copied</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Could the system have restarted">Could the system have restarted</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What might have caused">What might have caused</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can't have known">can't have known</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must not have received">must not have received</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might have had">might have had</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The last train departed at 10:05, and Lee's badge exited the station at 10:04. Lee <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must have left" data-hint="Use a strongly supported completed active event with the participle left." data-fix="Lee must have left on the last train.">choose</button> on the last train.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The autosave indicator was gray, and no new version appears in the history. The editor <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might not have saved" data-hint="Keep non-saving possible without treating it as certain." data-fix="The editor might not have saved the final paragraph.">choose</button> the final paragraph.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>No one answered at 4:00, but three people had appointments for 4:05. They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could have been waiting" data-hint="Infer a possible activity already in progress at that time." data-fix="They could have been waiting in the lobby.">choose</button> in the lobby.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The alarm was armed, the gate log shows no entry, and every window was locked. The building <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must have been closed" data-hint="Use have been plus an adjective for a strongly inferred past state." data-fix="The building must have been closed.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Two identical versions now exist, but the audit trail is incomplete. The file <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="may have been copied" data-hint="The affected file is the subject, so use a cautious modal-perfect passive." data-fix="The file may have been copied before the audit began.">choose</button> before the audit began.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The monitor went blank and then displayed a new startup time. Ask about one possible completed event: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Could the system have restarted" data-hint="Place the modal before the subject and keep have plus participle." data-fix="Could the system have restarted during the outage?">choose</button> during the outage?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The team knows the shutdown had a cause but has several possibilities. Ask for that possible cause: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What might have caused" data-hint="The wh-word is the subject of caused, so no extra subject or did is needed." data-fix="What might have caused the shutdown?">choose</button> the shutdown?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The policy was published after the decision, so the earlier committee <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can't have known" data-hint="The publication timeline rules out access to that later policy." data-fix="The earlier committee can't have known the later policy.">choose</button> its final wording.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The customer asks for the code that appeared clearly in the original message. A strong negative inference is that they <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must not have received" data-hint="Use full must not have for a strong inference of nonreceipt, without calling it impossible." data-fix="They must not have received the original message.">choose</button> the original message.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>The device stopped twice, but the diagnostic log is missing. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might have had" data-hint="After the modal, use have plus the participle had to infer a possible past possession or experience." data-fix="It might have had an intermittent power problem.">choose</button> an intermittent power problem.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Do not confuse identical-looking modal-perfect forms</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Could have + participle</span> has more than one use. The surrounding facts decide whether the outcome is unknown or known not to have happened.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Meaning</th><th>Context</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>epistemic possibility</td><td>the actual past route is unknown</td><td>The courier <b>could have taken</b> the service road.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>unrealized ability or opportunity</td><td>the facts establish that the action did not happen</td><td>We <b>could have restored</b> the backup, but we did not.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>counterfactual result</td><td>an unreal condition frames an alternative result</td><td>If we had checked, we <b>could have found</b> the error.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Nearby meanings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">Should have checked</span> evaluates a desirable past action. It does not estimate whether checking occurred unless the context says so.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Would have found</span> gives the expected result inside a counterfactual model. It is not an ordinary evidence-based guess about the actual past.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Had to check</span> reports past obligation or necessity. Deduction <span class="ex">must have checked</span> reports a conclusion.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Couldn't have opened it</span> can mean that opening was impossible or that the person lacked the ability. State the evidence or limitation so the listener can recover the intended meaning.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished actual-past uncertainty from unrealized opportunity, counterfactual result, evaluation, obligation, passive possibility, and process speculation.">
    <h3>Name the meaning before using the form</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Modal-perfect meaning choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a live past possibility">a live past possibility</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an unrealized opportunity">an unrealized opportunity</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a counterfactual result">a counterfactual result</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a past evaluation">a past evaluation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a strong past inference">a strong past inference</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a past obligation">a past obligation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a weak negative possibility">a weak negative possibility</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a strong negative inference">a strong negative inference</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a cautious passive possibility">a cautious passive possibility</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an ongoing possible activity">an ongoing possible activity</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The route log is missing, so <span class="ex">The courier could have taken the service road</span> expresses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a live past possibility" data-hint="The actual route is unknown and the service road was available." data-fix="Here, could have keeps one actual-past possibility open.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The team did not use the available backup. <span class="ex">They could have restored it at 9:00</span> expresses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an unrealized opportunity" data-hint="The context establishes that the available action did not happen." data-fix="Could have describes an unrealized opportunity here.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">If the team had checked the snapshot, it could have found the omission</span> gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a counterfactual result" data-hint="An unreal past if-clause creates an alternative world." data-fix="Could have found is a counterfactual result inside the alternative model.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">The team should have checked the snapshot</span> gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a past evaluation" data-hint="The speaker evaluates the desirable action after the fact." data-fix="Should have expresses evaluation or criticism, not probability.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Three matching records support <span class="ex">The transfer must have started at 8:00</span>, which is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a strong past inference" data-hint="The speaker concludes from converging records." data-fix="Must have gives a strong past inference.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The procedure required a supervisor's signature. <span class="ex">The team had to obtain approval</span> reports <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a past obligation" data-hint="Had to reports a requirement that existed in the past." data-fix="Had to reports past obligation, not deduction.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The mail log is incomplete. <span class="ex">The notice might not have arrived</span> expresses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a weak negative possibility" data-hint="Arrival and nonarrival both remain possible." data-fix="Might not have keeps nonarrival possible without ruling arrival out.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>A verified time record makes attendance impossible. <span class="ex">She can't have attended in person</span> gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a strong negative inference" data-hint="The known location directly contradicts attendance." data-fix="Can't have gives a strong negative inference from contradictory evidence.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The audit trail is incomplete, and two identical files exist. <span class="ex">The file may have been copied</span> gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a cautious passive possibility" data-hint="The file receives a possible action by an unidentified agent." data-fix="May have been copied is a cautious modal-perfect passive.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>At 8:08 the transfer had no completion entry. <span class="ex">It might have been running</span> gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an ongoing possible activity" data-hint="Have been plus -ing profiles a possible process in progress." data-fix="Might have been running presents an ongoing possible activity.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: keep weak have audible enough</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>U.S. spoken form</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>In connected speech, <span class="ex">have</span> is often weak /əv/: <span class="ex">must've</span> /ˈmʌstəv/, <span class="ex">might've</span> /ˈmaɪtəv/, and <span class="ex">could've</span> /ˈkʊdəv/. The content participle usually carries important stress: <span class="ex">must've LEFT</span>.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Could've</span> may sound like “could of,” but standard writing is always <span class="ex">could have</span> or <span class="ex">could've</span>. <span class="ex">Of</span> is not an auxiliary.</li>
      <li>Negative forms often keep the modal contrast clearer: <span class="ex">CAN'T have finished</span>, <span class="ex">MIGHT not have heard</span>. <span class="ex">Couldn't have</span> may sound like /ˈkʊdənəv/ in relaxed speech.</li>
      <li>Do not erase the form completely. A listener needs enough of <span class="ex">have</span>, <span class="ex">been</span>, the participle, and the context to distinguish <span class="ex">must leave</span> from <span class="ex">must have left</span>, and <span class="ex">might have copied</span> from <span class="ex">might have been copying</span>.</li>
      <li>Thought groups help separate evidence from conclusion: <span class="ex">The completion entry is missing | so it CAN'T have finished normally.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read weak have, completed and continuous viewpoint, negative deduction, must-not inference, and participle-stress listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You recovered five complete modal-perfect meanings from reduced U.S. speech rather than guessing from one stressed word.">
    <h3>Listen before opening the transcript</h3>
    <p>Ask your tutor to read the five lines naturally in order. Choose the complete wording and meaning you hear. Request one repetition if needed.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Past speculation listening choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must have left">must have left</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might have missed">might have missed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could have been waiting">could have been waiting</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can't have signed">can't have signed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must not have heard">must not have heard</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must leave">must leave</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The badge record is at 6:02, so she <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must have left" data-hint="Listen for weak have between must and the stressed participle left." data-fix="She must have left at six.">listen</button> at six.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The notice was small, so they <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might have missed" data-hint="Listen for uncertain might've before the completed participle missed." data-fix="They might have missed the notice.">listen</button> the notice.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>No one answered, but they <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could have been waiting" data-hint="Recover both been and -ing for a possible activity in progress." data-fix="They could have been waiting downstairs.">listen</button> downstairs.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The signature was added after his access ended, so he <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can't have signed" data-hint="Listen for the stressed negative modal and the participle signed." data-fix="He can't have signed that version.">listen</button> that version.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She asked for information that was announced twice, so she <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must not have heard" data-hint="Listen for full negative inference must not have, not a prohibition." data-fix="She must not have heard the announcement.">listen</button> the announcement.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    <details><summary>Tutor script and transcript</summary><ol><li>The badge record is at six oh two, so she must've LEFT at six.</li><li>The notice was small, so they might've MISSED it.</li><li>No one answered, but they could've been WAITING downstairs.</li><li>The signature was added after his access ended, so he CAN'T have signed that version.</li><li>She asked for information that was announced twice, so she must not have HEARD the announcement.</li></ol><p>Read the evidence and conclusion as separate thought groups on the second pass. Keep <span class="ex">have</span> weak but recoverable.</p></details>
  </div>

  <h2>Read a technical record without inventing a culprit</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Eastport Museum archive file</h3>
    <p>On Friday at 5:10 p.m., the museum saved the configuration for its Saturday archive transfer. The configuration included the Main Gallery folder but omitted the West Gallery folder. File L-07 was in Main Gallery; file L-08 was in West Gallery.</p>
    <p>On Saturday, the automated job began at 8:00 a.m. Ten of twelve image files reached Archive A. The process log shows L-07 entering the transfer queue at 8:06. The network monitor records a lost connection from 8:07 to 8:11. L-07 has no normal completion entry. A backup service created one partial encrypted package at 8:09.</p>
    <p>L-08 never entered the transfer queue. At 9:05, an audit found both missing files unchanged on the source drive. At 11:00, staff recovered L-07 from the partial backup and copied L-08 from the source drive. All twelve images were available by 11:18.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence limits:</b> The timing supports the possibility that L-07 was transferring when the network failed. It does not document the exact process state at 8:07. The configuration snapshot strongly supports the conclusion that L-08's folder was omitted. The record does not identify why the network connection failed, and it does not establish that one person caused either problem.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You reconstructed the Eastport record from exact times, queue evidence, configuration scope, recovery evidence, and stated limits without turning a hypothesis into fact.">
    <h3>Eight evidence-bound reading decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Eastport case-file choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="8:06">8:06</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the network interruption from 8:07 to 8:11">the network interruption from 8:07 to 8:11</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="it never entered the queue">it never entered the queue</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the Friday configuration omitted the West Gallery folder">the Friday configuration omitted the West Gallery folder</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a possible interruption during transfer">a possible interruption during transfer</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a strong inference that the folder was excluded">a strong inference that the folder was excluded</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a ruled-out completed normal transfer">a ruled-out completed normal transfer</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the record does not identify a cause for the network interruption">the record does not identify a cause for the network interruption</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The process log first places L-07 in the queue at <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="8:06" data-hint="Find the exact queue-entry time, not the job start or outage start." data-fix="L-07 entered the transfer queue at 8:06.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The timed event that makes an interrupted L-07 transfer plausible is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the network interruption from 8:07 to 8:11" data-hint="Choose the event that overlaps the interval after L-07 entered the queue." data-fix="The network interruption from 8:07 to 8:11 makes interruption plausible.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>L-08 can't have completed the automated transfer because <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="it never entered the queue" data-hint="A file cannot complete this automated route without first entering its queue." data-fix="L-08 never entered the queue.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The direct configuration evidence is that <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the Friday configuration omitted the West Gallery folder" data-hint="Use the saved settings snapshot rather than a later outcome." data-fix="The Friday configuration omitted the West Gallery folder.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">L-07 might have been transferring when the connection failed</span> expresses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a possible interruption during transfer" data-hint="The timing fits, but the exact process state is not recorded." data-fix="The claim presents a possible interruption during transfer.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><span class="ex">The settings must have omitted L-08's folder</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a strong inference that the folder was excluded" data-hint="The saved snapshot provides strong positive support." data-fix="Must have presents a strong inference that the folder was excluded.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span><span class="ex">L-07 can't have completed the normal transfer</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a ruled-out completed normal transfer" data-hint="The expected completion entry is absent, although a partial backup exists." data-fix="The normal completed-transfer explanation is ruled out.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The responsible final limit is: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the record does not identify a cause for the network interruption" data-hint="Do not assign a technical cause or a person when the file supplies neither." data-fix="The record does not identify a cause for the network interruption.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the reconstruction</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="file l-07 might have been transferring when the connection failed" data-hint="Start with the file, use might have been plus -ing for a possible process, and finish with the timed event." data-fix="File L-07 might have been transferring when the connection failed." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence keeps the L-07 process possible and locates it at the connection failure.">
    <h3>Builder 1: possible process</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the calibrated L-07 process hypothesis.</p><div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="when">when</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="file">File</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="transferring">transferring</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the connection">the connection</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="might">might</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="l-07">L-07</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="have been">have been</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="failed">failed</button></div><div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="file l-08 can't have entered the queue because its folder was excluded" data-hint="Use can't have plus entered, then state the configuration contradiction." data-fix="File L-08 can't have entered the queue because its folder was excluded." data-success-message="Correct. The negative deduction is tied to the excluded-folder evidence.">
    <h3>Builder 2: ruled-out event</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the L-08 negative deduction and its evidence.</p><div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the queue">the queue</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="because">because</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="entered">entered</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="was excluded">was excluded</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="file">File</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="can't have">can't have</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="its folder">its folder</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="l-08">L-08</button></div><div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the settings must have omitted the west gallery folder" data-hint="Place the evidence-based subject first, then must have and the participle omitted." data-fix="The settings must have omitted the West Gallery folder." data-success-message="Correct. The positive deduction preserves base have and the lexical participle omitted.">
    <h3>Builder 3: strongly supported cause</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the configuration conclusion.</p><div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the west gallery folder">the West Gallery folder</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="omitted">omitted</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the settings">The settings</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="must">must</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button></div><div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the broken layer</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="went" data-hint="After modal plus have, use the past participle of go." data-fix="The courier must have gone through the service entrance." data-why="Go changes to went in Past Simple but to gone after have." data-success-message="Correct. Modal plus have requires the irregular participle gone.">
    <h3>Repair 1: lexical participle</h3><p>The access log strongly supports the route. Tap the form that cannot follow <span class="ex">must have</span>.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="courier">The courier</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="must">must have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="went">went</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="entrance">through the service entrance.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="has" data-hint="A modal takes base have, even with a singular subject." data-fix="The server might have been copying the files." data-why="Might is the finite modal; the following auxiliary remains base have." data-success-message="Correct. The modal is followed by base have, not has.">
    <h3>Repair 2: auxiliary after the modal</h3><p>The process is possible, not confirmed. Tap the auxiliary with the wrong form.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="server">The server</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="might">might</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="has">has been</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="copying">copying the files.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="must" data-hint="L-08 never entered the queue, so the network interruption cannot explain both omissions." data-fix="The network interruption can't have caused both omissions because L-08 never entered the queue." data-why="Must have overstates and reverses the evidence relationship. The queue record rules the shared-cause claim out." data-success-message="Correct. The modal now follows the decisive queue contradiction rather than an attractive story.">
    <h3>Repair 3: evidence before confidence</h3><p>Tap the modal that makes an impossible shared-cause claim.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="network">The network interruption</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="must">must have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="caused">caused both omissions</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="queue">although L-08 never entered the queue.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="of" data-hint="The reduced sound /əv/ comes from the auxiliary have." data-fix="The backup could have captured part of L-07." data-why="Standard modal-perfect form is modal plus have plus participle. Of is a preposition, not the auxiliary heard in could've." data-success-message="Correct. The spoken reduction could've is written could have, never could of.">
    <h3>Repair 4: speech does not change spelling</h3><p>Tap the word that imitates the sound but breaks the grammatical form.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="backup">The backup</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="could">could</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="of">of</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="captured">captured part of L-07.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Say the inference before you reveal it</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Guided oral evidence updates</h3>
    <p>Read the full context, say one calibrated sentence aloud, and reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Two independent records strongly support an 8:00 start.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The transfer must have started at 8:00.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> The exact L-07 process state at 8:07 is unknown, but the timing fits an active transfer.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>L-07 might have been transferring when the connection failed.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> L-08 never entered the queue, so a completed automated transfer is impossible.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>L-08 can't have completed the automated transfer.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> The notice was available, but an incomplete mail log leaves nonreceipt possible.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The recipient might not have received the notice.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> The record gives no technical cause and identifies no responsible person.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The connection may have failed for several reasons; the record does not identify one.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice investigation without exposing private information</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to speculate about a real coworker, client, family member, medical event, disability, relationship, immigration case, legal dispute, financial loss, private message, location, password, disciplinary matter, or identifiable incident. Use Eastport, public information with reliable sources, or tutor-created fictional evidence cards. The skill is calibrated reasoning, not surveillance or accusation.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Evidence ladder:</b> Create one neutral fictional outcome and six evidence cards. Begin with two live possibilities. Add a clue that strongly supports one, then add a contradiction that rules another out.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Viewpoint switch:</b> Describe a completed event, a past state, an ongoing past activity, and a passive past event with four different modal-perfect forms.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Meaning switch:</b> Use <span class="ex">could have</span> once while the actual outcome is unknown and once when the context establishes an unrealized opportunity. Make the difference recoverable without labels.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Negative scale:</b> Use <span class="ex">might not have</span>, <span class="ex">must not have</span>, and <span class="ex">can't have</span> for three evidence relationships. Explain what would make you weaken or strengthen each claim.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Verification close:</b> End one reconstruction with what the evidence supports, what it does not establish, and the next record needed before any person or cause is named.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second evidence reconstruction</h3>
    <p>Use Eastport or another tutor-supplied fictional file. Start with at least six recorded facts and keep those facts grammatically separate from your conclusions. Give one strongly supported positive inference, two live possibilities, one weak negative possibility, one strong negative inference, one possible ongoing process, and one passive possibility. Include a question that requests missing evidence. Then reveal one new clue, revise at least one earlier claim, and distinguish speculative <span class="ex">could have</span> from either unrealized opportunity or a <span class="ex">should have</span> evaluation. Close with one evidence limit and one verification step. Use natural weak <span class="ex">have</span> without losing the participle.</p>
    <p><b>Success criteria:</b> Can the listener identify every recorded fact, the judgment time, the inferred event time, the evidence relationship behind each modal, completed versus ongoing viewpoint, active versus passive voice, negative strength, the meaning of <span class="ex">could have</span>, what changed after new evidence, and what remains unknown? Can you weaken a claim immediately when challenged with a missing record?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You calibrated support and contradiction, preserved negative nuance, separated could-have meanings, built continuous and passive forms, asked a complete question, and respected evidence limits.">
    <h3>Final check: defend the reconstruction</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
